---
import Layout from "@components/Layout.astro";
import PageHeader from "@components/PageHeader.astro";
import DecklistTooltip from "@components/DecklistTooltip.astro";
import WipAlert from "@components/WipAlert.astro";
import { Card } from "webcoreui/astro";
---

<Layout title="Intuition Guide - Replenish Guide"
    description="Master the art of Intuition in Replenish. Discover common pile patterns, engine setups, and complex situational plays to maximize your card selection.">
    <PageHeader
        title="The Intuition Guide"
        description="<strong>A few tips:</strong> Intuition is a skill-intensive card, and it might take some time to learn all the possible lines that the card enables, as it plays multiple critical roles throughout a game. A fundamental rule of Intuition is the tradeoff between immediacy and future availability: when you tutor for a non-combo piece (like removal or a sideboard card), you are effectively removing three copies of that card from your deck to guarantee access to one. Keep in mind also when you are building your deck that any card you intend to reliably fetch with Intuition requires you to run at least 3 copies in your 75."
        imageSrc="/src/assets/banners/intuition.jpeg"
        imageAlt="Intuition"
        imageCaption="Intuition by April Lee"
        isCard={true}
    />
    <WipAlert />
    <Card title="General Heuristics" titleTag="h2">
        <p>
            Timing is everything. Because <a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Intuition">Intuition</a> is an instant, you almost always want to cast it on your opponent's end step. This lets you untap with full mana available to resolve a lethal <a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Replenish">Replenish</a> or preserve interaction on your turn, granting your opponent a drastically compressed tactical window to react while gathering maximum information before committing.
        </p>
        <p>
            Navigating incomplete piles demands adaptability—if you desperately require a <a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Swords to Plowshares">Swords to Plowshares</a>, but have already drawn one with only two remaining in your library, construct a hybrid defensive structure such as Swords + Swords + <a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Parallax Wave">Parallax Wave</a>. Maintain strict mental tracking of remaining library allocations so you never cast Intuition only to discover you cannot assemble a three-of-a-kind guarantee.
        </p>
        <p>
            Finally, when fighting through permanent graveyard disruption like <a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Tormod's Crypt">Tormod's Crypt</a> or <a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Planar Void">Planar Void</a> post-sideboard, Intuition ceases functioning as a combo engine setup and immediately pivots into your ultimate removal tutor—searching for three copies of <a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Seal of Cleansing">Seal of Cleansing</a> to cleanly dismantle opposing hate prior to reloading your graveyard.
        </p>
    </Card>

    <Card title="Common Scenarios & Piles" titleTag="h2">
        <p>Below are primary championship configurations and strategic navigation heuristics:</p>

        <ul style="padding-left: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 3rem;">
            <li style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">
                <strong>Dumping Combo Pieces:</strong><br />
                The primary operational sequence. Use Intuition to deposit precise foundational enchantments directly into your graveyard—an ideal play when holding <a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Replenish">Replenish</a> paired with an active discard engine (<a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Attunement">Attunement</a> or <a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Frantic Search">Frantic Search</a>).<br />
                <em>Crucial Heuristic:</em> Because the opponent selects which card enters your hand, if an enchantment absolutely must reach the graveyard immediately, your pile must include at least two copies of it.<br />
                <strong>Standard Configurations:</strong> Opal + Decree + Wave, Opal + Opal + Wave, Opal + Opal + Decree, or Wave x3 (against explosive aggro).
            </li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">
                <strong>Tutoring Removal (<a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Swords to Plowshares">Swords to Plowshares</a> or <a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Seal of Cleansing">Seal of Cleansing</a>):</strong><br />
                Deployed when confronting lethal on-board threat clocks. Searching for <a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Seal of Cleansing">Seal of Cleansing</a> yields higher systemic synergy than Swords because discarded Seals naturally reanimate to the battlefield upon revolving your next <a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Replenish">Replenish</a>.<br />
                <strong>Standard Configurations:</strong> <a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Swords to Plowshares">Swords to Plowshares</a> x3, <a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Seal of Cleansing">Seal of Cleansing</a> x3.
            </li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">
                <strong>Guaranteeing Land Drops:</strong><br />
                Search for three lands to guarantee continuous colored mana development, ensure critical land drops on schedule, or proactively accelerate mana production by grabbing three copies of <a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Ancient Tomb">Ancient Tomb</a>. While utilized less frequently, it prevents fatal developmental stumbles.<br />
                <strong>Standard Configurations:</strong> <a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Ancient Tomb">Ancient Tomb</a> x3, <a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Skycloud Expanse">Skycloud Expanse</a> x3, <a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Plains">Plains</a> x3.
            </li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">
                <strong>Finding a Discard Engine:</strong><br />
                When retaining complete combo redundancy plus <a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Replenish">Replenish</a> in hand without an operational discard outlet, utilize Intuition to secure immediate card selection engines.<br />
                <em>Note:</em> Grabbing three copies of <a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Attunement">Attunement</a> requires substantial mana commitments across subsequent turns, so verify sufficient developmental time before opting out of instantaneous instant-speed cantrips.<br />
                <strong>Standard Configurations:</strong> <a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Frantic Search">Frantic Search</a> x3, <a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Attunement">Attunement</a> x3.
            </li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">
                <strong>Finding Sideboard Silver Bullets:</strong><br />
                Fetch three exact copies of a meta-breaking sideboard tool to paralyze opposing combo engines, dismantle countermagic, or dominate mirror interactions.<br />
                <strong>Standard Configurations:</strong> <a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Meddling Mage">Meddling Mage</a> x3, <a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Abeyance">Abeyance</a> x3, <a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Tsabo's Web">Tsabo's Web</a> x3.
            </li>
        </ul>
    </Card>
    <DecklistTooltip />
</Layout>
